  "title": "An expired reservation still runs the work unslotted while the daemon is answering",
  "detail": "When a reply says the queued reservation expired (`{acquired:false, expired:true}`, which happens after a daemon restart, for example), the ordinary path throws 'gate-slot lease expired'. The outer catch then warns and runs `work()` unslotted, which is the case #554 forbids, because the daemon is clearly reachable. Reproduction (Codex, fake client and clock): reply `{id:'q', acquired:false}`, advance 250 ms, then reply `{id:'q', acquired:false, expired:true}`. With maxWaitMs 60000 the work runs unslotted with the warning. With maxWaitMs 0 the expiry check is skipped and the caller polls 'q' forever, even after capacity is free, which is a regression from main. Fix: for ordinary callers, treat an expired reservation as 'request a new reservation' (clear the id and keep waiting under the same responsive rule). Agent-test lanes keep their LeaseRejected. Add tests for both maxWait values."
 },
